UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pedantic-arts-residency-and-research-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Arts Residency and Research Grant 2027 (Pittsbur
 gh)
DESCRIPTION:Pedantic Arts Residency opens applications for its Summer 2027 
 and Fall 2027 programmes in Pittsburgh: two four-week residency cohorts an
 d two research grants. THE RESIDENCY houses three creatives at a time (a v
 isual artist\, an organizer and a writer) in a collective four-week progra
 mme that emphasizes exploration\, exchange and community connection over p
 roduction. Residents get free furnished housing in a shared apartment\, a 
 USD 2\,000 stipend to cover living expenses (half on arrival\, half on com
 pletion)\, a Pittsburgh-based guide working in their field\, tickets and i
 nstitutional passes\, and introductions across the city's creative communi
 ty. THE RESEARCH GRANT invites an individual visual artist\, curator or wr
 iter for a one- to two-week independent stay to conduct Pittsburgh-related
  research\, with a free private bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment\, a USD 
 500 or USD 1\,000 honorarium usable at the grantee's discretion\, and help
  establishing relevant connections. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be 18 or 
 older and not Pittsburgh residents at the time of application\; travel cos
 ts are the participant's own. Residency attendance and staying in the prov
 ided housing are required. APPLICATION: applications are free until 28 Sep
 tember 2026 at 23:59 EST\; a USD 20 fee applies from then until the final 
 deadline of 15 October 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts R
 esidency\nLocation: Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA. Open to non-Pittsburg
 h residents aged 18 or older\; travel is self-funded.\nAward: Residency: f
 ree furnished housing in a shared apartment plus a USD 2\,000 living stipe
 nd (half on arrival\, half on completion). Research Grant: a free private 
 bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment plus a USD 500 or USD 1\,000 honorarium 
 at the grantee's discretion. Application free until 28 September 2026\, th
 en USD 20.\nDuration: Residency: four weeks\, Summer 2027 or Fall 2027 coh
 orts. Research Grant: one to two weeks.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.org/
 announcements/open-call-for-residents-and-grantees-submit-by-october-15th/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/announcements/open-call-for-residents-and-gran
 tees-submit-by-october-15th/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA. Open to non-Pittsburgh residents 
 aged 18 or older\; travel is self-funded.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:surels-place-residency-2027-winter@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Surel's Place: Month-Long Artist Residency (September 202
 6 deadline)
DESCRIPTION:Surel's Place is a residency in Garden City\, Idaho with a two-
 fold mission: to give artists the time\, shelter and professional support 
 their work deserves\, and to give the public accessible art experiences in
 cluding performances\, readings\, exhibits and workshops. In exchange for 
 the residency\, artists offer art experiences back to the community. OPEN 
 TO professional visual\, literary and performance artists: painters\, writ
 ers\, musicians\, architects\, filmmakers\, choreographers\, any artist wh
 o needs a place to focus. LIMITS: because of the property's constraints an
 d proximity to neighbours\, it cannot accommodate loud or very messy proce
 sses such as welding or blacksmithing. The organisers also note that predo
 minantly conceptual work\, work that must be explained to attract a viewer
 \, may not be met with as much enthusiasm by the jurors\, and that they we
 lcome artists who want to connect with an audience. Each cycle\, one of th
 e five residencies includes outreach to local schools through the PARTNER 
 Schools Program. REQUIREMENTS: maintain residence at the home and studio (
 no studio-use-only residencies)\; use the residency in a focused way towar
 ds a stated goal with no other employment or work happening simultaneously
 \; visual artists give a show of and/or lecture about their residency work
 \, writers give a reading and discussion session\; all artists offer at le
 ast one public workshop (2 to 3 hours\, minimal lecturing)\; visual artist
 s donate one piece of art to Surel's Place for future fundraising\; writer
 s allow Surel's Place to publish a free-standing excerpt of their residenc
 y work in books\, broadsides\, posters or similar. SALES COMMISSION applie
 s as set out in the funding notes. HOUSE RULES: the non-smoking requiremen
 t is non-negotiable and any evidence of smoking is grounds for early termi
 nation. Partners are welcome but children and pets cannot be accommodated\
 , no more than two adults may live there during a residency\, and partners
  wanting concurrent residencies must apply and be accepted separately. ELI
 GIBILITY: applicants must be 25 or older and non-smokers. APPLY by email t
 o info@surelsplace.org with the online Artist in Residence application plu
 s\, for VISUAL ARTISTS\, a cover letter introducing yourself and saying wh
 y you want to be at Surel's Place specifically\, a proposal including a wo
 rkshop outline\, a CV\, electronic images of 4 to 6 pieces of work and an 
 image list (title\, size\, medium\, year)\; for LITERARY applicants\, cove
 r letter\, proposal with workshop outline\, CV and PDF work samples with y
 our name and page number in the top right corner (fiction\, prose or scrip
 t no more than 10 typed double-spaced pages\; poetry no more than six poem
 s and no more than 10 pages)\; for OTHER MEDIUMS\, cover letter\, proposal
  with workshop outline\, CV and electronic samples (contact Surel's Place 
 to discuss sample requirements for your medium). Applications are reviewed
  by juries of accomplished artists\, writers and fine arts professionals\,
  and all applicants are notified by email.\n\nOrganisation: Surel's Place\
 nLocation: In person in Garden City\, Idaho\, USA (Boise area). Residents 
 must live at the home and studio\; no studio-only residencies.\nAward: Fre
 e rent\, utilities and wi-fi\, a living stipend of USD 100 per week\, a US
 D 300 travel stipend\, use of well-maintained bicycles\, free or discounte
 d tickets to art events and movies\, marketing through Surel's Place chann
 els\, and event hosting including logistics and installation help. Each re
 sident also gets a local host to orient them and host their public events.
  No application fee. NOTE: Surel's Place takes a commission on sales arisi
 ng from the residency\, 35% of retail price on artwork\, 45% on ticketed e
 vents that are offsite or need contracted services (calculated after admin
 istrative expenses)\, and 15% on books\, CDs or other merchandise tangenti
 al to the artist's medium. A surcharge may apply to cover additional utili
 ty costs if a partner joins.\nDuration: One month (longer may be possible 
 if justified in the application). The 1 September deadline covers residenc
 ies in January to May of the following year\, beginning four months after 
 the deadline\; the 1 March deadline covers July to November of the same ye
 ar.\n\nMore: https://surelsplace.org/month-long-residencies/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://surelsplace.org/month-long-residencies/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:In person in Garden City\, Idaho\, USA (Boise area). Residents mus
 t live at the home and studio\; no studio-only residencies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-michalski-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan Michalski Foundation: Writers Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Residency for writers and translators at the Jan Michalski Foun
 dation in Montricher\, Switzerland\, set in seven distinctive 'cabin' modu
 les hanging from an openwork canopy\, offering conditions to start\, conti
 nue or finish a writing project. Around forty authors from around the worl
 d (emerging to established) are hosted each year. Open to all kinds of wri
 ting and all languages\, with priority given to literary writers and trans
 lators\; other disciplines are welcome as long as literature is at the hea
 rt of the project. Residencies are for individuals or pairs working on a c
 ommon project (e.g. a writer and a translator). A percentage of residencie
 s are dedicated to nature writing. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a private cabin for i
 ndependent living (a separate cabin per person for pairs\; one accessible 
 cabin for reduced mobility)\, travel costs to and from home\, a weekly all
 owance of CHF 400\, breakfast and lunch\, electric bikes\, and daytime lib
 rary access. ELIGIBILITY: no age or nationality restrictions\; beginners a
 ccepted\; one application per year\; former residents may not reapply (fam
 ilies\, children and pets cannot be accommodated). Stays cannot be split i
 nto multiple periods. Selection is by a panel chaired by Vera Michalski-Ho
 ffmann\, assessing the literary quality of the project\, the candidate's b
 ackground\, and whether the stay length matches the project scope. APPLICA
 TION: online in English or French (work excerpts may be in any language)\;
  the 2027 form is open 2 June to 31 August 2026\; selected candidates anno
 unced December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Jan Michalski Foundation for Writing
  and Literature\nLocation: Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lau
 sanne and Geneva)\nAward: Weekly allowance of CHF 400\, plus travel costs 
 to and from home covered\, accommodation in a private cabin\, and breakfas
 t and lunch provided. Electric bikes and library access included.\nDuratio
 n: Two weeks to three months (first 2027 residents arrive mid-January 2027
 )\n\nMore: https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lausanne and Geneva)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hkbu-iww-writers-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hong Kong Baptist University: International Writers' Work
 shop 2027 (Writers-in-Residence)
DESCRIPTION:International Writers' Workshop (IWW) at Hong Kong Baptist Univ
 ersity (HKBU)\, founded in 2004\, has hosted over 150 writers from more th
 an 60 countries. The 2027 Writers-in-Residence Programme runs 26 February 
 to 25 March 2027 and culminates in the IWW Literary Festival on the theme 
 'Inheritance'. Writers are encouraged to share a piece of writing in conve
 rsation with the festival theme. ELIGIBILITY: have at least one published 
 book\; currently reside outside of Hong Kong\; have a functional command o
 f English or Chinese (Mandarin or Cantonese). WHAT IWW PROVIDES: round-tri
 p economy class airfare\; accommodation on HKBU's campus for 4 weeks\; a p
 er diem. DEADLINE: 14 August 2026. APPLY via the IWW HKBU call for applica
 tion (PDF).\n\nOrganisation: International Writers' Workshop (IWW)\, Hong 
 Kong Baptist University (HKBU)\nLocation: HKBU campus\, Hong Kong\nAward: 
 Round-trip economy class airfare\; accommodation on HKBU's campus for 4 we
 eks\; a per diem. No application fee.\nDuration: 4-week residency\, 26 Feb
 ruary to 25 March 2027\, culminating in the IWW Literary Festival on the t
 heme 'Inheritance'\n\nMore: https://iww.hkbu.edu.hk/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iww.hkbu.edu.hk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
LOCATION:HKBU campus\, Hong Kong
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-writing-in-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Writing in Residency
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Writing in Residency programme provides residenc
 y opportunities (for example Traduki in Southeast Europe or Art Omi) for a
 uthors and translators to develop or research projects. Applicants must ha
 ve prior professionally published work. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection
  to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular a
 rtistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swi
 ss connection. WHAT IS OFFERED: travel and accommodation costs (varying by
  destination)\, plus childcare support of up to CHF 1\,000 per month for a
 pplicants with caregiving responsibilities. Submission deadline 1 Septembe
 r (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro He
 lvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors and trans
 lators\; residencies at partner locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeas
 t Europe\, Art Omi).\nAward: Travel and accommodation costs (vary by desti
 nation)\; childcare support up to CHF 1\,000 per month for applicants with
  caregiving responsibilities. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency to 
 develop or research a project\; deadline 1 September.\n\nMore: https://pro
 helvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and translators\; residencies at partner
  locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeast Europe\, Art Omi).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wheeler-centre-next-chapter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Wheeler Centre: The Next Chapter 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Next Chapter is The Wheeler Centre's flagship writing progr
 am\, designed to elevate Australian stories that are underrepresented and 
 to nurture a new wave of writers to tell them. Each fellow receives a AUD 
 $15\,000 stipend and is paired with a handpicked mentor for a twelve-month
  period to progress a major writing project. Fellows also receive a reside
 ncy at Varuna\, The National Writers' House\; an end-of-year publishing in
 tensive at The Wheeler Centre\; and meaningful opportunities to connect wi
 th peers\, agents\, publishers\, and readers. One fellowship place is dedi
 cated specifically to a poet: The Malcolm Robertson Fellowship. 2027 judge
 s: Melissa Lucashenko\, Micaela Sahhar\, Cher Tan\, and Melanie Saward. EL
 IGIBILITY: Australian writers. No specific genre restrictions stated\; the
  program focuses on stories that are not currently being told and voices t
 hat are underrepresented. TIMELINE: submissions open 2 June 2026\; submiss
 ions close 31 July 2026 (5pm)\; 2027 Next Chapter Fellows announced 10 Nov
 ember 2026. Questions: thenextchapter@wheelercentre.com. Apply at https://
 www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter.\n\nOrganisation: The Wheeler Centr
 e\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Na
 tional Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Whe
 eler Centre.\nAward: AUD $15\,000 stipend per fellow. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 12 months.\n\nMore: https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chap
 ter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Nationa
 l Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Wheeler 
 Centre.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tartu-city-of-literature-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260921T041126Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tartu UNESCO City of Literature Residency for Writers and
  Translators\, Autumn 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Estonian Literary Society\, which coordinates Tartu UNESCO 
 City of Literature\, runs an international residency programme for writers
  and translators that has hosted authors from Slovenia\, Ireland\, Hungary
 \, the USA\, the UK\, Ukraine and Canada since 2017. This is the open call
  for the autumn 2026 slot: one resident stays two months in the Karl Risti
 kivi residency apartment in Tartu\, working on their own writing or transl
 ation while connecting with the local literary scene. WHAT THE RESIDENCY O
 FFERS: a EUR 600 monthly stipend\, travel reimbursement up to EUR 350\, fr
 ee accommodation\, a local support coordinator to help arrange cultural en
 gagements\, and opportunities to perform and present at literary events. T
 he autumn period covers the interdisciplinary literary festival Crazy Tart
 u on 12 to 14 November\, and the resident is offered a slot to perform the
 re alongside writers\, poets\, musicians and artists from Estonia and abro
 ad. ELIGIBILITY: open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian liter
 ature of any nationality\; applicants need an upper-intermediate level of 
 spoken English\, at least one published book\, screenplay\, theatre script
  or translation from Estonian into another language\, a demonstrable inter
 est in Estonian culture and literature\, a willingness to take part in loc
 al literary activities\, and a commitment to working on their own literary
  project during the stay. HOW TO APPLY: complete the online application fo
 rm linked from the residency page and upload a fragment of up to five page
 s of a published text (in Estonian or English) or of a published translati
 on. SELECTION: made by a committee representing the Estonian Literary Soci
 ety\, the Estonian Writers Union\, the Estonian Literary Museum and the Ta
 rtu Literature House Foundation. Results are announced before 15 September
  2026. The programme's stated aims are to enhance international exchange\,
  diversify the local literary scene\, introduce new foreign authors and th
 eir work to Estonian readers\, and build lasting connections beyond the re
 sidency period. Questions: Marja Unt\, eks@kirjandus.ee. Deadline 1 Septem
 ber 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Estonian Literary Society (Eesti Kirjanduse Sel
 ts)\, Focal Point for Tartu UNESCO City of Literature\nLocation: Tartu\, E
 stonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian literature wor
 ldwide.\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 600 for the two-month stay (EUR 1\,
 200 in total)\, plus reimbursement of travel costs up to EUR 350. Free acc
 ommodation is provided in the Karl Ristikivi residency apartment\, which h
 as a bedroom\, living room\, kitchen\, bathroom and exhibition room. One r
 esident is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months\, 15 Octobe
 r to 15 December 2026\, with some flexibility on exact dates\n\nMore: http
 s://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tartu\, Estonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estoni
 an literature worldwide.
